> Topic: 10-dimension visual comparison rubric, unified `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` deviation grading, per-screen evidence table, and visual verdict rules.

Rules **V6**, **V7**, **V9**, **V10**, and **V12**.

---

## 1. 10-Dimension Visual Comparison Checklist (`V6`, `V7`)

Compare every captured screenshot (`.png`) side-by-side against the approved visual reference (`.superpowers/sources/<ISSUE-ID>/figma/<stem>-SNN.png` and `design.md` `## UI/UX mapping`):

| # | Dimension | Verification Check | `BLOCKER` (`FAIL`) | `MAJOR` (`FAIL`) / `MINOR` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | **Layout & Hierarchy** | Screen regions appear in approved order (`app bar` → `header/filter` → `content` → `footer/CTA`); grid columns match viewport | Missing/reordered region or overlapping surfaces | `MAJOR`: tablet 2-column layout rendered as stretched 1-column |
| **2** | **Spacing & Alignment** | Padding, margins, and gaps match token scale; edges and baselines align | Render overflow (`overflowed by N pixels`), clipped text/controls | `MINOR`: 2–4px non-destructive spacing variance |
| **3** | **Typography** | Font family, size/weight hierarchy, and multi-line wrapping/ellipsis on long data | Truncated critical data (prices, IDs, status) or broken hierarchy | `MAJOR`: unguarded long text breaking row/card height |
| **4** | **Color & Tokens** | Surface, text, border, and semantic colors (`success`, `warning`, `danger`) use approved theme tokens | Hardcoded color breaking theme/contrast; wrong semantic color | `MINOR`: subtle shade variance inherent to kit widget |
| **5** | **Shared Components** | Approved UI kit / design-system components used per `design.md` mapping | Raw/custom widget built where an approved kit component fits without a `Core gap` (`D-NN`) | `MAJOR`: wrong component variant (e.g. primary vs secondary) |
| **6** | **Icons & Media** | Approved icon set, sizes, aspect ratios, and image shimmer/placeholder states | Missing icon, broken asset, or misleading icon semantics | `MINOR`: minor icon size variance |
| **7** | **4 Mandatory UI States** | `Loading`, `Content`, `Empty`, and `Error` (with retry/recovery) all rendered and verified | Any of the 4 states missing, blank, or crashing | `MAJOR`: loading spinner causes layout jump |
| **8** | **Responsiveness & Safe Area** | Confirmed viewports (`.superpowers/ux/viewports.json`), portrait/landscape orientation, notch/home-bar/keyboard insets | Control hidden under notch, home indicator, or keyboard | `MAJOR`: horizontal overflow on target viewport |
| **9** | **Copy & Formatting** | Exact labels, messages, units, and date/currency formatting from spec | Untranslated keys or copy that alters business meaning | `MINOR`: minor punctuation nuance |
| **10** | **Accessibility Basics** | Touch targets (`>= 48x48dp` Android / `>= 44x44pt` iOS), contrast (`>= 4.5:1`), focus/keyboard navigation | Unreadable contrast or untappable control (`< 36dp`) | `MAJOR`: touch target below `48x48dp` / `44x44pt` |

- **Decisions (`D-NN`)**: When a visual difference from the mockup occurs because an approved UI kit component enforces its own styling (`D-NN`), record it as `ACCEPTED (D-NN)` — never fail code for following an approved `D-NN`.

